{
  "slug": "geometric-series-oq-07-oq-01-oq-01-oq-01-oq-01-oq-03-oq-02",
  "title": "The Fourth Column of the Eulerian Triangle: ⟨n,3⟩ = 4ⁿ − (n+1)·3ⁿ + C(n+1,2)·2ⁿ − C(n+1,3)",
  "phase": "COMPLETED",
  "status": "completed",
  "tier": "B",
  "path": "full",
  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "Prove a division-free closed form for the fourth column of the Eulerian triangle: for all n, 6·⟨n,3⟩ = 6·4ⁿ − 6·(n+1)·3ⁿ + 3·n·(n+1)·2ⁿ − (n−1)·n·(n+1), equivalently ⟨n,3⟩ = 4ⁿ − (n+1)·3ⁿ + C(n+1,2)·2ⁿ − C(n+1,3) (OEIS A000498), the k=3 instance of the inclusion–exclusion formula ⟨n,k⟩ = ∑_{i=0}^{k} (−1)ⁱ·C(n+1,i)·(k+1−i)ⁿ.",
    "plain": "A fully machine-checked closed form for the fourth column ⟨n,3⟩ of the Eulerian triangle, extending the parent's columns 0, 1, 2. Stated over ℤ cleared of its /6 to avoid division: 6·⟨n,3⟩ = 6·4ⁿ − 6·(n+1)·3ⁿ + 3·n·(n+1)·2ⁿ − (n−1)·n·(n+1), equivalently ⟨n,3⟩ = 4ⁿ − (n+1)·3ⁿ + C(n+1,2)·2ⁿ − C(n+1,3) (OEIS A000498) — the third nontrivial case of the inclusion–exclusion formula ⟨n,k⟩ = ∑_{i=0}^{k} (−1)ⁱ·C(n+1,i)·(k+1−i)ⁿ. The proof is an induction on n driven by the definitional single-step Eulerian recurrence ⟨n+1,3⟩ = 4·⟨n,3⟩ + (n−2)·⟨n,2⟩, feeding in the parent's eulerian_col_two; the only subtlety is the truncated ℕ subtraction (n−2), which is harmless because ⟨0,2⟩ = ⟨1,2⟩ = 0. Verified against rows ⟨3,3⟩=0, ⟨4,3⟩=1, ⟨5,3⟩=26. 0 axioms, 0 sorries.",
    "whyMatters": []
  },
  "knownResults": {
    "proven": [
      "eulerian_col_three: the closed form 6·⟨n,3⟩ = 6·4ⁿ − 6·(n+1)·3ⁿ + 3·n·(n+1)·2ⁿ − (n−1)·n·(n+1) for the fourth column of the Eulerian triangle (OEIS A000498), the next case after the parent's columns 0–2 and the third nontrivial instance of the Eulerian inclusion–exclusion formula",
      "The induction is closed by the definitional recurrence ⟨n+1,3⟩ = 4·⟨n,3⟩ + (n−2)·⟨n,2⟩ together with the parent's column-two formula; the truncated ℕ subtraction (n−2) is reconciled with (n−2 : ℤ) by case-splitting n ∈ {0,1,≥2}, where for n ∈ {0,1} the vanishing of ⟨n,2⟩ makes the contribution zero either way"
    ],
    "open": [],
    "goal": "Prove a division-free closed form for the fourth column of the Eulerian triangle: for all n, 6·⟨n,3⟩ = 6·4ⁿ − 6·(n+1)·3ⁿ + 3·n·(n+1)·2ⁿ − (n−1)·n·(n+1), equivalently ⟨n,3⟩ = 4ⁿ − (n+1)·3ⁿ + C(n+1,2)·2ⁿ − C(n+1,3) (OEIS A000498), the k=3 instance of the inclusion–exclusion formula ⟨n,k⟩ = ∑_{i=0}^{k} (−1)ⁱ·C(n+1,i)·(k+1−i)ⁿ."
